# Image request: 0003 image tool editor

- **From:** Claude Code
- **Created:** 2026-11-14 20:42 -05:00
- **Purpose:** Show the full editor with node GUIs in an image tool, with the large GUI of the
  selected node in the inspector. It also corrects mockup 1: compile layers, icons and labels.
- **Output:** `docs/mockups/0003-image-tool-editor-v1.png`
- **Size:** 3200 x 2000 if the tool can make it. Else the largest landscape size that it can
  make. Do not upscale a smaller image. Report the real size.
- **Background:** opaque.
- **References:** `docs/mockups/mockup-1-main-editor-colored-headers.png`: keep its layout and
  density. `docs/mockups/mockup-9-smart-material-editor.png` and `docs/gui-visual-guide.md`:
  use their theme and palette, not the blue cast of mockup 1.
  `docs/mockups/0001-node-gui-widget-kit-v1.png` and
  `docs/mockups/0002-node-gui-gallery-v1.png`: use their widgets and node GUIs.
- **Spec:** 0 (mockup errors), 4.3 (Node GUI), 7.3 (Layer display), 15.2 (Layout and docking),
  15.3 (Visual rules), 15.4 (Inspector). Common rules and icons: `docs/mockup-plan.md`.
- **Previous request:** none

## Brief

The full Patina window on Windows 11, with the layout of mockup 1: the top bar, the Layers panel
on the left, the graph in the center, the inspector on the right, the bottom panel and the
status bar. The graph zoom is 125%, so that the node GUIs stay readable.

Top bar: the blue faceted Patina logo of the guide, "Image Pipeline / Main Graph", **LIVE** with
a green dot, undo, redo, "125%", fit, grid, **Run**, **Pause**, **Bake** and a **Views** menu.
**Bake** is dim, because no node is in the slot. The Windows caption buttons are at the far
right. The active tab of each panel uses the amber accent #DFA64B.

Left panel: the tabs **Layers** and **Project**. **Layers** is active, with exactly two rows:

- **Base**: a green dot with its icon, "Ready", "Built in 41 s".
- **Slot**: gray, "Empty".

Graph, all frame domain, wired in a row from left to right: **Load Image** (thumbnail),
**Denoise**, **Apply Curve**, **Gradient Map** (compact GUI as in 0002) and **Preview** (large
thumbnail).
**Curve Editor** (compact GUI as in 0002) sits above Apply Curve. Its `Curve` output wires into
the `Curve` input of Apply Curve. Curve Editor is selected, with a pink outline #DE8FBA, the
lighter shade of its header color. All nodes are Ready, and each node shows its run time.

Header colors from the families of the guide, with neutral node bodies: Load Image input amber
#6B4B1E, Denoise processing teal #175C59, Apply Curve, Curve Editor and Gradient Map curve
magenta #71344F, Preview output purple #59366F.

Inspector:

- Header: the stateful node-kind icon, **Curve Editor**, "Stateful node", the path "Main Graph /
  Curve Editor", a layer badge **Base**, a green Ready dot with its icon, "Run 0.02 ms" and an
  expand button. Curve Editor has the full size, so its node header shows the expand button
  too.
- Under the header, the large GUI of Curve Editor: a large canvas with the tone curve, a
  histogram, a 4 x 4 grid and five points, one of them selected. Under the canvas: the
  segmented control **RGB R G B**, number fields "In 0.42" and "Out 0.55", a toggle
  **Histogram** and a button **Reset**. It is the same GUI as in the node, at the large size.
- Under the GUI, the tabs **Parameters**, **Code** and **Logs**. **Code** is active and shows
  the start of the node code, with line numbers:

```rust
#[node(full_gui, color = "#71344f")]
pub struct CurveEditor { points: Vec<[f32; 2]> }

impl CurveEditor {
    pub fn ui(&mut self, ui: &mut Ui) {
        if ui.button("Reset").clicked() { self.points.clear(); }
        let canvas = ui.canvas(240.0, 140.0);
```

The moment: the user edited Curve Editor, then made no change for the fuse time. The engine
fused the node back into the base (spec 7.2). The code stays open, but the node is not in the
slot, so the status bar shows "Fused" and **Bake** is dim.

Bottom panel: the tabs **Logs**, **Output** and **Debug**. **Logs** is active, with three lines.

Status bar: on the left, a green dot, "Ready" and "0 errors". On the right, "Project: Image
Pipeline" and "Fused".

Avoid: layer toggles, colored layer squares, a **+** button in the Layers panel, the Rust logo,
a **Compare** tab, and labels that mix build and run times, such as "Compiled 12.8 ms".

## Exact text

Required: the top bar labels, the Layers panel rows, the node titles, the inspector header, the
GUI labels, the code above, the tab names and the status bar text.

Illustrative: the log lines, for example "20:42:10  Graph run in 3.1 ms". The image content.

## Acceptance

- The Layers panel shows exactly the **Base** and **Slot** rows, with no toggles and no **+**
  button.
- The Curve Editor GUI shows twice: compact in the node and large in the inspector, with the
  same design.
- The inspector header shows "Main Graph / Curve Editor" and the badge **Base**. No Rust logo.
- **Bake** is dim, and the status bar shows "Fused".
- The bottom panel has only the **Logs**, **Output** and **Debug** tabs.
- Build time and run time are separate labels.
